  "name": "Elder Wand procs its target debuff from Crystal Cannon and Shatter Echo as well as Artificer's Wand (#12461)",
  "contract": "Elder Wand 560129 applies aura 42 (proc trigger spell) on Elder Wand 560128, a target debuff (+3% Artificer's Wand damage taken per stack, up to 10 stacks, never a player buff). Its initial spell_proc row masked SpellFamilyMask2 to 512 (Artificer's Wand 561064) with AttributesMask 0, omitting two other Chronomancer ranged wand attacks (SpellFamilyName 28, DmgClass 3) that both Spell.dbc and live Ascension combat logs show proc 560128: Crystal Cannon (704481 -> periodic-triggered 560134, SpellFamilyFlags[2] = 4096, without SPELL_ATTR3_NOT_A_PROC so it requires PROC_ATTR_TRIGGERED_CAN_PROC = 2) and Shatter Echo (572417 / 804503 / 807950-807953, SpellFamilyFlags[2] = 20). Updating SpellFamilyMask2 to 4628 (512 | 4096 | 20) and setting AttributesMask |= 2 enables both while keeping Chance at the tooltip's 30% and keeping non-wand ranged Singularity Core (804437, SpellFamilyFlags[0] = 1024) excluded. The scenario runs 10 Singularity Core control casts (0 procs), 10 Crystal Cannon channels (20 landed 560134 hits, P(no proc) = 0.70^20 = 0.08%), and 20 Shatter Echo casts (20 hits with Echo Fragment 804455 held, P(no proc) = 0.70^20 = 0.08%), asserting monotonic Elder Wand proc and target debuff application deltas for each phase and verifying 560128 never appears as a buff on the Chronomancer.",
